hermes v0.23.0: a vault card fill asks for consent before it knows the
checkout can take a card.

Symptom: on a checkout whose card inputs sit only in a processor's
cross-origin iframe, browser_vault action=fill prompted the user to confirm
the card, was approved, then failed with "No payment form fields were
found"; every agent retry prompted again.

Fix: inspect the bound page before the prompt and refuse with
no_payment_fields when it has no card number control. The fill still
re-inspects inside the backend's fill_context after consent, so only
controls stamped after the prompt can be written.
hermes-vault-payment-iframe-fill.patch (applied after this one) widens the
pre-consent check to card numbers in a processor's card frame.

Upstream: NousResearch/hermes-agent#126889 (open), commit d64330bcc9 as is,
on top of hermes-vault-generate-password.patch (the login classify of that
patch kept in the extracted _inspect_page). Drop when merged.

